# Analyze-and-report includes plots

**Incident (2026-09-14c):** `full_im150_meancell` was scored with eval
tables only. User had to ask for S/I/M, prior, and behavior overlays.

When the user asks to **analyze and report** newly fitted Stage B / joint
`weights_run_*` models, numbers alone are incomplete.

## Required overlays (each run dir)

Same shared-stim protocol as the eval (`bps=20`, stim seed **12345**,
stim from regular **s101** unless the campaign says otherwise). Put
files **in that run directory** (plots-live-with-data). Do not use
repo `figs/`.

| Overlay | Typical files |
|---------|----------------|
| I/M traj vs data | `IM_pre.svg` / `.png` (alias of `IM_pre_fit_gi…`) |
| P traj | `P_fit.svg` / `.png` |
| retinal S vs contrast (`L_S`) | `S_fit.png` (if that term exists) |
| prior-distance I/M (+ S sidecar if `include_stim`) | `prior_effects.svg` / `.png` |
| ITI mean traj (S stim L/R; I/M choice L/R) | `S_iti.svg` / `I_iti.svg` / `M_iti.svg` (+ `.png`) |
| act-prior psychometric + RT combined + RT split | `psychometric_model_vs_data_actprior/` |

S ITI splits previous-trial **stim** L vs R; I and M split previous-trial
**choice** L vs R. Two signed pop-diff traces per figure. Included from
`plot_best_fit_results.plot_one`.

Reuse the campaign driver if it exists (`_tmp_full_s_prior_plots.py`,
`_tmp_*_actprior_rt.py`, `plot_best_fit_results.plot_one`). Journal
may **link** the ONE paths.

Every SVG must have a PNG sibling. Do **not** skip plots because eval
tot already exists.
